tle":"FEMA Documentation Support","description":"Detailed record-keeping and documentation that meets FEMA requirements for disaster reimbursement. We help you recover eligible costs."},{"title":"Community Recovery Partnership","description":"We work alongside emergency management agencies, utilities, and contractors to support comprehensive community recovery efforts."}],"faqs":[{"question":"How quickly can you respond to a disaster?","answer":"We maintain emergency response teams and equipment staged in strategic locations. For predicted events like hurricanes, we pre-position resources. For sudden disasters, we typically mobilize within 24-48 hours."},{"question":"Do you handle hazardous materials from disasters?","answer":"Yes, we're equipped to handle household hazardous waste, construction debris with asbestos concerns, and other regulated materials that commonly appear in disaster cleanup. All disposal follows proper regulatory protocols."},{"question":"Can you help with FEMA reimbursement documentation?","answer":"Absolutely. We provide detailed documentation of all work performed, including load tickets, tonnage reports, GPS tracking, and photo documentation that meets FEMA eligibility requirements."},{"question":"What types of disasters do you respond to?","answer":"We respond to hurricanes, tornadoes, floods, ice storms, wildfires, and other natural disasters. We also support cleanup from man-made emergencies and industrial incidents."},{"question":"Do you work with insurance companies?","answer":"Yes, we provide documentation and work directly with insurance adjusters when needed. Our detailed records support claims processing and help expedite settlements."}]}],["$L7","$L8","$L9"],"$La"]}],{},null,false,false]},null,false,false]},null,false,false]},null,false,false],"$Lb",false]],"m":"$undefined","G":["$c",[]],"S":true}
